Tell the page when graphics are unavailable

When neither WebGPU nor WebGL2 can be initialized, the platform never
launches the application and only appends a line of text to the page, which a
page that loads the application has no way to notice. Dispatching a
gpui:graphicsunavailable event on the window, with the error as its message,
lets such a page explain the failure in its own way.

